[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0c001871d201b205016a21af26ec708199ba95f71c374a848f","text":"Implemented a minimal tscircuit RP2040 board in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx:1). It uses `routingDisabled`, local RP2040/flash component definitions, built-in primitives, USB-C, 3.3 V power, QSPI flash, 12 MHz crystal, SWD/debug, boot/reset, and GPIO headers. No tscircuit registry components were imported.\n\nValidation:\n- `npm run typecheck` passes.\n- `tsci check schematic-placement` passes with no placement issues.\n- `tsci build` exits 0 and writes `dist/index/circuit.json`, but reports expected missing physical trace DRC items because routing is disabled, plus some JLCPCB supplier footprint mismatch warnings.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: `supplierPartNumbers` requires arrays (`{ jlcpcb: [\"C...\"] }`), while examples showed strings.\n- Wasted most time: making schematic-placement happy around verbose net labels; `schDisplayLabel` on explicit traces did not clear those warnings, but named nets did.\n- Helpful docs/tooling changes: clearer `routingDisabled` build/DRC expectations, current supplier part number examples, and a searchable list of valid footprinter strings.\n- Friction points: unsupported `crystal5x3` footprint was only caught at build time, and schematic checker fixes sometimes caused new overlap suggestions on rerun.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019e938c-1a1e-7620-aee4-267e29f5c525","turnId":"019e938c-1a3b-7f71-8284-03f1a67c6f26","completedAtMs":1780592428452}}
